  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The prossimo passage",
   "texto": [
    "It is formed with the present of **avere** (**ho, hai, ha, abbiamo, avete, hanno**) plus the **participio**: **Ieri ho parlato con Sara** (yesterday I spoke with Sara). It is equal to both the perfect composite preterito («I've spoken.») and the simple perfect preterito («I talked.») in Spanish.",
    "Attention! **Ho** also means «I have» (**ho fame**, I'm hungry), but before a participle it works as a temporary assistant."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Regular training of the participle",
   "texto": [
    "**-are → -ato** (parlare → parlate), **-ere → -uto** (ricevere → ricevuto), **-ire → -ito** (dormire → dorto, capire → capito).",
    "With the «avere» auxiliary, the participle ends in **-o** and does not change with the subject: **Io ho parlato, noi abbiamo parlato**."
   ]
